Q1. Why Comparable and Comparator interfaces required in java ?
👉 We know that for primitive data types (like int, char, double) Java already provides Arrays.sort() or Collections.sort() to sort them easily because their natural order is already defined.
But when we deal with custom objects (like Employee, Student, Product), Java doesn’t know how to compare two objects (by id? by name? by salary?) That’s why we need Comparable and Comparator interfaces.
because They allow us to define our own sorting logic.

Q2. Difference between Comparable and Comparator?
